course: dictionary
lesson: 9050
title: Sleepiness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sleepiness is the feeling of being sleepy, when you are tired and want to sleep. The ending -ness turns the describing word sleepy into a noun, a name for a feeling. You may already know sleepy, so you can use it to unlock sleepiness.
explain: Context gives clues. «Caffeine in cola, tea and energy drinks blocks sleepiness» tells you these drinks stop you feeling sleepy. Blocks is the clue: it means stops something from happening.
explain: Sleepiness can also be a warning sign. «After a head bump, signs like sleepiness, being sick or a bad headache can appear hours later and need a doctor.» Sleepiness is listed with being sick and a headache, so after a head bump it can mean something is wrong.
fact: Sleepiness means the feeling of being sleepy and tired.
fact: The ending -ness turns a describing word like sleepy into a noun.
fact: Caffeine in cola, tea and energy drinks blocks sleepiness, and about half of it is still in the body about 5 hours later.
fact: Some older hay fever tablets cause sleepiness, so pharmacists can suggest non-drowsy kinds.
fact: Drivers must never drive when they feel sleepy.
exercise: «Caffeine blocks sleepiness.» What does blocks mean here? | Makes it bigger | *Stops it from happening | Sings loudly | Paints a wall
exercise: What is sleepiness? | A kind of medicine | Sleeping very late at night | *The feeling of being sleepy and wanting to sleep | A big soft bed
exercise: A head bump can bring signs like sleepiness and being sick. What should you do? | Ignore it, it always goes away | Drink a cola and carry on | *Tell a doctor, because signs can appear hours later | Wait a week and see
test: Why can pharmacists suggest non-drowsy hay fever tablets? | *To help people avoid sleepiness from their medicine | To stop people taking any medicine | To sell more cola | To make people sleepier
test: A driver feels sleepiness coming on. What is the safe choice? | *Do not drive | Turn up the music and keep driving | Drive faster to get home sooner | Drink a strong energy drink and carry on
exam: The word sleepiness ends in -ness; what does that ending tell you? | It shows the word is a question | It means more sleepy than before | *It turns sleepy into a noun, a name for a feeling | It makes the word a verb, an action
